  greetings:
  - Evening, Detective. Mind the floor, it's wet.
  - Still here? Me too.
  aboutSelf: Been down here all night with the furnace. She's older than me and twice as mean. Don't tell Alma I'm in; she'll have me fixing the lobby door again.
  aboutTown: Semblance. Never been. My cousin delivers feed up that way. Says the dogs there don't bark at strangers, and he doesn't like it.
  seenAnythingStrange: Biscuit won't go past the third row of shelves. Sits and stares at the wall. Dogs know things. Then again, she's half blind.
  foundersDay: 
  gossip:
  - title: About Alma Reyes
    response: Alma feeds my dog when she thinks I'm not looking. Thirty years and she thinks I don't know. She's a good one.
